[block'ORD-0011-app-on-rust'
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-001','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-001/EMS-001.pgml']
  [onlyif'ORD-0009 closed','ORD-0010 closed']
  [tgt'the browser app talks to the Rust engine behind one switch, and glyph-ui.js changes only at its transport']
  [cnst'the protocol is ADR B: the page posts one request line to /engine on its own origin, and serve-dev.js relays it to glyph-engine with --engine rust, or to glyph-protocol.js']
  [cnst'the transport is a Core of the same shape as GlyphCore: the twelve calls go through /engine, and the tables, esc, xesc and walk stay the JS core']
  [nt'run is synchronous: the transport asks with a synchronous request, the one reading that leaves glyph-ui.js untouched; question 9 of the return stays open for the Regent']
  [nt'parse cannot send the live tree: the transport rebuilds segments from the full envelope, and buildXml and serializeAST ask toXML and toAST of the source the segments came from']
  [nt'the engine answers with the repository stores; the templates a page merges stay on the JS path, as question 11 of the return reads it']
  [ins'the switch is one query parameter of the page, engine=relay; without it the page runs on the JS core as it does today']
  [val'the app on the Rust engine','the app drives the 114 sources through Rust with the same bytes as through JS, and the JS path still works']
];
